MIXED body lines only on base (15): Build Your XI hands you a formation, then a slot machine assigns a random club or country to every position. Your job is naming a player from that exact team who fits each slot. | When the eleventh name lands, an AI referee grades the lineup and writes a short scouting report, then a season report plays a full year out with your XI: league finish, points, trophies and a top scorer. No two teams ever come out alike. | Choosing one of six formations | Spinning a club or country per slot | Tap a position. The spinner shows which club or national team that slot is locked to. | Typing a player who fits the slot | Type a player from that team who fits. The game verifies the answer before it counts. | Hate an assignment? Reroll it for a different team. | Fill all 11 slots, check the role fit, chemistry and balance tiles under the pitch, then submit for the AI rating. | Scoring chemistry and the offline backup judge | If the AI judge is unreachable, a built in offline judge grades you instead, so a run never dead ends. | Naming goalkeepers from small clubs | Small club on the wheel? Goalkeepers are easy to name, elite wingers are not. | A rating headline, a short written analysis of your picks, and your role fit, chemistry and balance tiles. Under it comes a season report: a squad rating out of 100, where you finish in a 20 team league, points, trophies and a top scorer, plus how your defence, midfield and attack compare and what role fit, chemistry and balance were each worth in poi
MIXED body lines only on head (17): Choose a formation and fill 11 slots. Mixed is the default clubs and countries mode. Club year draft uses 11 different clubs, not nations, and records from one year. | Mixed keeps its AI verdict and season report. Club year draft uses your selected values and ages for a fictional season. Missing either leaves the completed XI unrated. | Choosing Mixed or Club year draft | Choose a recorded year from 2004 to 2026 before the formation. It stays fixed for the draft. | Drawing teams and choosing an empty slot | Tap any empty position on the pitch. Fill it with a player who matches the current team and fits that position. | Searching or browsing matching player records | Type a name and choose a suggestion that fits the slot. Club year picks must match both club and recorded year. | Tap Browse players to see matching Club year records, or type to narrow them. Records may be incomplete, not a full squad or proof of every appearance. | No matching record? Try another name or reroll. Club year rerolls change the club, keeping the year. | A RECORDED GOALKEEPER EXAMPLE | Choose 2010, tap GK and use Browse players. A goalkeeper record from the current club in 2010 can fill that slot; a record only from a different year cannot. | Fill all 11 slots and check the role fit, chemistry and balance tiles under the pitch. Mixed uses its usual evaluation when you submit. | Chemistry and the Mixed backup judge
